# Source Information: bunka.org

## URLs
- **Main Index (Searchable Table):**
  https://www.bunka.go.jp/kokugo_nihongo/sisaku/joho/joho/kijun/naikaku/kanji/joyokanjisakuin/index.html
- **Appendix (付表) Parent Page:**
  https://www.bunka.go.jp/kokugo_nihongo/sisaku/joho/joho/kijun/naikaku/kanji/index.html

## Extraction Rules
- **漢字 (Kanji):** Primary key. If "新字体（旧字体）" format is used, the first character is the key.
- **康熙 (Kouki):** The character inside parentheses in the 漢字 column. Empty string if none.
- **音訓 (Readings):** 
    - Separated into "音" (On) and "訓" (Kun) lists.
    - All readings go into a "常" (Joyo) bucket to match Jitenon compatibility.
- **付表 (Appendix):**
    - Scraped from the Fuhyo section.
    - Formatted as a dictionary/object: `{"Word": "Reading"}`.
- **備考 (Remarks):** Raw text from the Remarks column.

## Target JSON Structure (bunka.json)
```json
{
  "明": {
    "康熙": "",
    "読み": {
      "音": {
        "常": ["メイ", "ミョウ"]
      },
      "訓": {
        "常": ["あかり", "あかるい", "あかるむ", "あきらか", "あける", "あく", "あかす"]
      }
    },
    "備考": "",
    "付表": {
      "明日": "あす",
      "明後日": "あさって"
    }
  }
}
```
